== Important Commands:
=== Sail: 

`sail <heading> <distance>`

 Use this command to move around the map. You can use the direction and distance to sail to your desired location.

=== Inventory:
`inventory / bag / i`

Use this command to check your inventory. You can also use `bag` or `i` as a shortcut.

=== Open Bag/ Category/ Chest

`open <bag/category/chest>`

Use this command to open your bag (does the exact same thing as inventory), a category, or a chest.

=== Eat

`eat <item>`

Eat an item from your inventory. A sailor needs to keep his strength up! Food heals you.

=== Drink

`drink <item>`

Drink something from your inventory. Drinking liquor can give you a buff but may reduce your accuracy causing you to miss some of your attacks.

=== Equip

`equip <item>`

Equip an item from your inventory. Some equipment might come in handy in fights or provide armor to reduce damage taken.

=== Status

`status`

Check your current status and see how you're holding up.

=== Help

`help`

Display the list of available commands and their usage.

=== Quit

`quit`

End your voyage and leave the game. Hopefully not before reaching Otaniemi!

== HOW TO NAVIGATE:

The Entire game is based on a real nautical map of the Strait of Finland. You can use a divider or a ruler to navigate the map. I have added a scale of nautical miles to the map to help you navigate.

You can use the sail command to navigate the map. Each line on the bottom map shows you the direction and distance you have to sail for. 0 represents north, 90 represents east etc. The island of Sirens and Tokyo Tower are not mandatory to finish the game, you can just rush to Otaniemi and fight the final boss. It will affect the final score drastically though.

The game will tell you if you are close to some landmark and if you can see it from farther away. You can use this information to navigate the map and find your way to Otaniemi. But you still cannot see the coastline as there is dense fog in the strait.

You can only land at certain locations. You can see the locations you can land at on the map as the colour purple.

The game requires really good orienteering skills to navigate the map.

